    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the duplicate-telephone rejection in the owner creation endpoint.\n\n**Change:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, in `addOwner`.\n\nThe method already normalizes the incoming telephone by stripping non-digit characters. I added a check right after normalization (and before saving): it scans all existing owners, normalizes each stored telephone the same way, and if any match the new owner's normalized telephone, it returns `409 CONFLICT` instead of persisting.\n\n```java\nowner.setTelephone(telephone);\nboolean telephoneInUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .map(Owner::getTelephone)\n    .filter(existing -> existing != null)\n    .map(existing -> existing.replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\"))\n    .anyMatch(telephone::equals);\nif (telephoneInUse) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\nthis.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);\n```\n\nThis normalizes both sides of the comparison so numbers stored in any format still collide correctly, and satisfies both acceptance tests: duplicate normalized telephones \u2192 409, distinct telephones \u2192 2xx.",
